  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Kruisjassen. Logic: Trick-taking with turned trumps. Key: Trump J=20, 9=14. Must overtrump when possible. Last trick = 5 pts.',
    Player: 'Kruisjassen is a Dutch trick-taking game for 4 players in partnerships. The last card dealt determines trump. Trump Jack (20 pts) and Nine (14 pts) are especially valuable. Need 100 of 146 points to score. First to 11 game points wins.',
    objective: 'Win tricks containing high-value cards. Score game points by reaching point thresholds with your partner.',
    gameplay: "1. **Leading**: Player to dealer's left leads to first trick. Any card may be led.\n2. **Following Suit**: If a non-trump is led, players with that suit must either follow suit OR play a trump. A non-trump of a different suit can only be played if the player has no cards of the led suit.\n3. **Trumping Rules**: When playing a trump on a non-trump lead, it must be higher than any trumps already played to the trick. A lower trump can only be played if the player has no option (hand consists entirely of lower trumps).\n4. **Trump Led**: If a trump is led, other players must play trumps if they have them. Any trump may be played - no requirement to play higher.\n5. **Winning Tricks**: Highest trump wins, or if no trumps, highest card of led suit. Winner leads to next trick.",
    keyRules: [
      'Trump Jack is worth 20 points, Trump Nine is worth 14 points',
      'Last trick is worth 5 points',
      'Total points per deal: 146',
      'Need 100+ card points to score 2 game points',
      'Win all tricks to score 5 game points',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Four players in fixed partnerships, two against two. Partners sit opposite each other.',
      deck: '32-card French-suited pack (7 through Ace in each suit).',
      equipment: '32-card French-suited pack (7 through Ace in each suit).',
      dealing: "Dealer shuffles, offers to player on left to cut, then deals: 3 cards each, then 2 cards each, then 3 cards each. The last card (dealer's last card) is placed face up to determine trump suit, then taken into dealer's hand. Each player has 8 cards.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Leading**: Player to dealer's left leads to first trick. Any card may be led.\n2. **Following Suit**: If a non-trump is led, players with that suit must either follow suit OR play a trump. A non-trump of a different suit can only be played if the player has no cards of the led suit.\n3. **Trumping Rules**: When playing a trump on a non-trump lead, it must be higher than any trumps already played to the trick. A lower trump can only be played if the player has no option (hand consists entirely of lower trumps).\n4. **Trump Led**: If a trump is led, other players must play trumps if they have them. Any trump may be played - no requirement to play higher.\n5. **Winning Tricks**: Highest trump wins, or if no trumps, highest card of led suit. Winner leads to next trick.",
